    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n53632" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καστορ-ίδες</span></b> , αἱ, a
		famous Laconian breed of <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>hounds</i>, said to be first reared by Castor, <i><span class="en">
				<u>AP</u>
				6.167
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				Agath.
			</span></i>), cf. <i><span class="en">
				Poll.
				5.39
			</span></i>:—also <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καστόριαι</span></b> 
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κύνες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					X.
					<u>Cyn.</u>
					3.1
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>sea-calves, seals</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Opp.
				<u>H.</u>
				1.398
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ael.
				<u>NA</u>
				9.50
			</span></i>.</div>
